 "notice": {
  "head": "Maple Street Bakery Stays Open After Rent Fight",
  "text": "When Marta, who owns the Corner Bakery on Maple Street, announced the shop might close, the block reacted within hours. Maple Street is a [[tight-knit]] place: people lend tools, water each other's plants, and notice a strange car by morning. Some neighbors were [[wary]] of the landlord's opening offer — a one-year lease at nearly double the rent — and a few had [[an inkling]] that he already had a buyer. The local blog [[fanned the flames]] with a post about “greedy developers,” and by evening people were talking about a rent strike. Marta begged them not to [[blow the dispute out of proportion]]. “He is not a villain,” she said. “We just don't [[see eye to eye]] on the numbers.” A petition with two hundred signatures [[ruffled a few feathers]] at city hall, but the morning crowd — retirees, students, off-duty nurses — was hardly a [[conducive]] audience for staying calm: they had saved the hardware store in 2019, and they wanted a fight. Marta, who has [[a knack for]] keeping a room friendly, hosted meetings in the back room for two weeks. She heard everyone out, even the retired lawyer who [[grasped at straws]] to find a loophole in the lease, and the teenagers who [[ribbed]] her about her “corporate lawyer voice.” A city planner friend [[shed light on]] a zoning rule that allows a café on the ground floor, and a crowdfunding page pulled eleven thousand dollars [[out of thin air]]. The final two months were [[all-consuming]] — Marta called them “a second job I did not apply for” — and the campaign ran [[at the expense of]] her sleep. In the end the landlord signed a five-year lease. The new wooden sign, carved by a neighbor, [[does justice to]] the place, and on Sunday mornings the whole block [[basks in]] the smell of cardamom buns. The shop sits two doors [[off the map]] of every tourist guide, which suits everyone just fine. Marta says the fight gave the street [[closure]]: “We [[held firm to]] the plan, and the plan held.”",
